#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281829 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "517f2054-008e-54eb-89dd-5f0a09e1f881" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Cubic Polynomial Given Three Real Roots and a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "054c5af9-f22f-5aee-84ee-d1fe6af40e15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{3}+8{x}^{2}-36x-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281831} {:answer/id #uuid "02d64dd8-9ffb-5057-a345-ed1074e866dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-18x-36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281832} {:answer/id #uuid "18fe48b6-fc53-552c-bc6a-686f1a50953a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{3}+8{x}^{2}-36x-72" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281833} {:answer/id #uuid "484f8fdc-0eb0-5949-a210-0b1927a1eb4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{3}+8{x}^{2}-9x-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281834} {:answer/id #uuid "70da238b-5ac0-53a8-badc-d5c9b380e5e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}+18x-72" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281835}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "18fe48b6-fc53-552c-bc6a-686f1a50953a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{3}+8{x}^{2}-36x-72" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281833} :answer-field/id #uuid "b946e7ba-9790-5fcf-9684-08e62e179d46" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281830}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fcd56ce7-673a-5e4c-a842-541a666d3fe8" :question/math-academy-id "q-104458" :question/problem "The cubic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=-3,$ ${x}_{2}=-2,$ and ${x}_{3}=3,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $4.$ Find $P(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our cubic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}=-3,$ ${x}_{1}=-2,$ and ${x}_{3}=3,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=4,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) & =4(x-(-3))(x-(-2))(x-3) \\\\  & =4(x+3)(x+2)(x-3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(x+3)(x+2)(x-3) & =4({x}^{2}+5x+6)(x-3) \\\\  & =4({x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}+5{x}^{2}-15x+6x-18) \\\\  & =4({x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}-9x-18) \\\\  & =4{x}^{3}+8{x}^{2}-36x-72.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=4{x}^{3}+8{x}^{2}-36x-72.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281836 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "517f2054-008e-54eb-89dd-5f0a09e1f881" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Cubic Polynomial Given Three Real Roots and a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b7b79a8-bd7d-5421-861f-a35d03d95d6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281838} {:answer/id #uuid "38e9bc78-4057-531d-8c84-04ac59c4b9ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281839}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "38e9bc78-4057-531d-8c84-04ac59c4b9ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281839} :answer-field/id #uuid "3a2afe4d-ae4d-56b7-9a8e-785946d6dc98" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281837} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ceee8d75-1d60-5b63-ae81-002955f5003c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281841}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ceee8d75-1d60-5b63-ae81-002955f5003c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281841} :answer-field/id #uuid "a1210025-284b-5067-af6f-34c4151e1aad" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281840} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7ffa7955-34de-58dd-b06c-a6ae3642d7a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "55" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281843}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7ffa7955-34de-58dd-b06c-a6ae3642d7a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "55" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281843} :answer-field/id #uuid "58cbcbdd-d460-5c86-8fb7-df9201b203e9" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281842} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "af8c0a6b-d844-5c10-b7b8-0b75148b59f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281845}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "af8c0a6b-d844-5c10-b7b8-0b75148b59f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281845} :answer-field/id #uuid "0cf3be30-5389-5e81-98ea-ae68a35ce809" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281844}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "590f3038-6cc4-5c97-85c0-ebec225d6230" :question/math-academy-id "q-316619" :question/problem "The cubic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=1,$ ${x}_{2}=-3,$ and ${x}_{3}=4,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $5.$ Find $P(x).$\n\n$P(x)=$\n{{field-1}}${x}^{3}\\,-$\n{{field-2}}${x}^{2}\\,-$\n{{field-3}}$x\\,+$\n{{field-4}}" :question/worked-solution "Since our cubic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}=1,$ ${x}_{2}=-3,$ and ${x}_{3}=4,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=5,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) & =5(x-1)(x-(-3))(x-4) \\\\  & =5(x-1)(x+3)(x-4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(x-1)(x+3)(x-4) & =5({x}^{2}+2x-3)(x-4) \\\\  & =5({x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}+2{x}^{2}-8x-3x+12) \\\\  & =5({x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-11x+12) \\\\  & =5{x}^{3}-10{x}^{2}-55x+60.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=5{x}^{3}-10{x}^{2}-55x+60.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281846 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "517f2054-008e-54eb-89dd-5f0a09e1f881" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Cubic Polynomial Given Three Real Roots and a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e4c645a7-6e88-5972-b95f-905dac795ff5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281848}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e4c645a7-6e88-5972-b95f-905dac795ff5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281848} :answer-field/id #uuid "91791d0a-1066-5c42-b09c-9cb09d183694" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281847} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10c26c3e-2747-5197-ad23-a2ed18872e4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281850}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "10c26c3e-2747-5197-ad23-a2ed18872e4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281850} :answer-field/id #uuid "6bac3080-51d6-5bbf-b341-0d56be3ea619" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281849} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "760a6ca5-e3eb-547b-b1ce-767c2123969f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281852}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "760a6ca5-e3eb-547b-b1ce-767c2123969f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281852} :answer-field/id #uuid "20b89ba4-b596-516d-8f05-c3c0e495998e" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281851} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2933e7f1-ebb8-52f6-b1b0-a983d26a9cc0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281854}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2933e7f1-ebb8-52f6-b1b0-a983d26a9cc0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281854} :answer-field/id #uuid "40817d4a-1275-5ff8-aef6-04cef1d3a688" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281853}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b79b1845-4a56-5456-a000-eb06d5845200" :question/math-academy-id "q-316621" :question/problem "The cubic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=-4,{x}_{3}=1,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $2.$ Find $P(x).$\n\n$P(x)=$\n{{field-1}}${x}^{3}\\,+$\n{{field-2}}${x}^{2}\\,+$\n{{field-3}}$x\\,-$\n{{field-4}}" :question/worked-solution "Since our cubic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}=-4,$ ${x}_{2}=-4,$ and ${x}_{3}=1,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=2,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) & =2(x-(-4))(x-(-4))(x-1) \\\\  & =2(x+4)(x+4)(x-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(x+4)(x+4)(x-1) & =2({x}^{2}+8x+16)(x-1) \\\\  & =2({x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+8{x}^{2}-8x+16x-16) \\\\  & =2({x}^{3}+7{x}^{2}+8x-16) \\\\  & =2{x}^{3}+14{x}^{2}+16x-32.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=2{x}^{3}+14{x}^{2}+16x-32.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281855 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e4bb90c5-2794-5657-8f0b-45eb64873e03" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Cubic Polynomial Given One Real Root, Two Complex Roots, and a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "091f1f95-cef9-59b7-b7f9-1415cc9f5aff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281857} {:answer/id #uuid "a541f8ff-b62d-5e66-a809-6d0299be5a9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281858}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a541f8ff-b62d-5e66-a809-6d0299be5a9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281858} :answer-field/id #uuid "6dbdfc33-1e58-5242-8633-fda746b517e3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281856} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2162cc48-61f0-5b5c-b430-32b49357ae0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281860}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2162cc48-61f0-5b5c-b430-32b49357ae0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281860} :answer-field/id #uuid "19c06412-5cae-5797-897d-bdb5c92ef289" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281859} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98939d20-aade-57be-a048-e1e7c4db19fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281862}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98939d20-aade-57be-a048-e1e7c4db19fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281862} :answer-field/id #uuid "72a2f2ed-5eff-58bb-bfec-92ee85b2fd15" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281861} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e6538d37-a939-5af4-8d52-2f192dd54fc5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281864}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e6538d37-a939-5af4-8d52-2f192dd54fc5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281864} :answer-field/id #uuid "a70f3f5c-4515-5830-8325-e90e481a964b" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281863}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a501a88c-c742-55d1-9428-8cda49f09e51" :question/math-academy-id "q-316649" :question/problem "The cubic polynomial $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=-5,{x}_{2,3}=\\pm 2\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $5.$ Find $f(x).$\n\n$f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}${x}^{3}\\,+$\n{{field-2}}${x}^{2}\\,+$\n{{field-3}}$x\\,+$\n{{field-4}}" :question/worked-solution "Since $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=-5$ and ${x}_{2,3}=\\pm 2\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=5,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =5(x-(-5))(x-2\\text{i})(x-(-2\\text{i})) \\\\  & =5(x+5)(x-2\\text{i})(x+2\\text{i})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(x+5)(x-2\\text{i})(x+2\\text{i}) & = \\\\ 5(x+5)({x}^{2}-(2\\text{i})^{2}) & = \\\\ 5(x+5)({x}^{2}+4) & = \\\\ 5({x}^{3}+5{x}^{2}+4x+20) & = \\\\ 5{x}^{3}+25{x}^{2}+20x+100 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=5{x}^{3}+25{x}^{2}+20x+100.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281865 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e4bb90c5-2794-5657-8f0b-45eb64873e03" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Cubic Polynomial Given One Real Root, Two Complex Roots, and a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "201c6278-7349-5fcd-8d3d-50191307ca04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281867}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "201c6278-7349-5fcd-8d3d-50191307ca04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281867} :answer-field/id #uuid "b12deaa4-cb34-525a-8ae8-02dd21b65c52" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281866} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d2840503-ce0b-5918-8349-edf8ae2b4dba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281869}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d2840503-ce0b-5918-8349-edf8ae2b4dba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281869} :answer-field/id #uuid "068d1b3d-9cd6-5ce6-9816-9ec16c2cfbdd" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281868} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9c01ee05-a997-5ef6-9dca-0abe4ae30cea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "112" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281871}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9c01ee05-a997-5ef6-9dca-0abe4ae30cea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "112" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281871} :answer-field/id #uuid "0cd42360-fc09-5525-b898-248e077c1284" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281870} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4884c860-f659-554c-a527-edbfbc04fccd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "112" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281873}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4884c860-f659-554c-a527-edbfbc04fccd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "112" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281873} :answer-field/id #uuid "71124992-2f8f-5062-9e65-c7f08f220f8b" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281872}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "77e4d2d6-3fba-5e93-9f55-7ff26fc310fe" :question/math-academy-id "q-316704" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981281/assets/ce15895aa3a0f7e7cbea820e06a3c56aadef1d440b59120db17c5df394970adb.png)\n\nThe Argand diagram above shows the roots of a cubic polynomial $f(x).$\nFind $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the cubic term is $-7.$\n\n$f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}${x}^{3}\\,+$\n{{field-2}}${x}^{2}\\,-$\n{{field-3}}$x\\,+$\n{{field-4}}" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=1$ and ${x}_{2,3}=\\pm 4\\text{i}.$ Additionally, we're given that the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=-7.$ Therefore, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =-7(x-1)(x-4\\text{i})(x-(-4\\text{i})) \\\\  & =-7(x-1)(x-4\\text{i})(x+4\\text{i})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-7(x-1)(x-4\\text{i})(x+4\\text{i}) & = \\\\ -7(x-1)({x}^{2}+x(4\\text{i})-x(4\\text{i})-(4\\text{i})^{2}) & = \\\\ -7(x-1)({x}^{2}+16) & = \\\\ -7({x}^{3}+16x-{x}^{2}-16) & = \\\\ -7{x}^{3}+7{x}^{2}-112x+112.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=-7{x}^{3}+7{x}^{2}-112x+112.$"}]}
